WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.470
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.470
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.410
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.410
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.980
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.920
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.940
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.940
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.380
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.380
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.150
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.150
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.430
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.430
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.870
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.870
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:45.460
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:45.460
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.920
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.920
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.990
I can say love

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.720
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.720
It overflows with love.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.720
will you love me?

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.330
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.330
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.280
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.280
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.840
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.840
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.490
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.490
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.500
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.180
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.380
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.070
This is too much!

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.890
I can't contain myself!

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.890
Is it really that funny?

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.660
Uh oh!

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.020
What is it?

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.290
Kenneth Barl!

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.830
Rajau Ga Waura!

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.400
Y-Yamada Seina!

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.860
Initiating check.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.380
Good, you're all here.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.050
Tomorrow is the academy's entrance ceremony.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.000
Make sure that you get plenty of rest.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.800
Yes, sir!

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.590
Even though it's routine,
roll call sure is nerve-wracking.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.810
I know.{You got that right.} I don't think I'll ever get used to it.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.800
They do this everyday?

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.810
You bet. Everyday until you graduate.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.940
And I hear that a lot of people
who've graduated can't break the habit

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.980
of standing up straight in their
room at this time every night.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.510
No! I don't wanna turn out like that!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.820
No way! I don't think I could take it!

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:51.580
I see. I guess dorm life can be tough.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.790
Where you goin'?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:57.790
I thought I'd get to bed early
like the instructor said.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.220
What are you talkin' about, Seina-kun?

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.130
The night's still young.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.360
What's wrong, Seina-kun?!

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.370
I-I don't think we should be doing this.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.300
Come on, are Earthlings
that serious of a species?

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.770
That's strange, I heard they
were no different than us.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.880
What if someone finds us?!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.310
Don't worry! All we have to do
is fool the sensors in our room!

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.410
Which is precisely why I borrowed your NB.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.080
Everyone knows all the best parties are in the middle of the night!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.890
That's why we're sneaking out!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.580
We're going to a party?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.190
That's right! The likes of
which you've never seen before!

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.900
Lots of people from all over the galaxy gather at this academy.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.990
Each race has its own unique
customs, religions, and beliefs,

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.900
so naturally each one
has its own special day.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.030
Holidays, I guess you could call them.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.240
So everyday there's a new festival
or party going on somewhere!

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.740
E-Everyday?!

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.910
Yup. And they're big parties!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:18.120
The perfect chance to hook up with
beautiful ladies from all over space!

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.620
Wait! Stop!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.640
What's the matter?

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.340
Somebody's used our route.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.420
Damn. Who'd be out walking 
around this late at night?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.990
We're in no position to
criticize others about that,

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.620
but our only option now is
to take an alternate route.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.660
Gotcha.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.390
Seina, change of route.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.180
Hey!

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.900
Um, I don't think I can do this.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.730
Let's open this up and go through.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.100
I'm telling you, I'm not really...

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.000
Roommates do things together!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.400
Okay, okay.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.940
Now, then,

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.620
this is the most dangerous
part when leaving the dorms.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.740
Dangerous?

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:59.460
If you're spotted by
the surveillance system...

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.250
If you're spotted?

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.510
This happens to you.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.530
Observe!

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.340
You're given a lovely gift, a mark which
can neither be described nor shown on TV!

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.050
No way!

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.370
Incidentally, when you
get ten of these marks,

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.200
you win a trip around the
galaxy aboard a GP freighter,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.970
where you get to work
as head restroom cleaner!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.440
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.490
You still not done?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.530
Is everything okay?

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.990
Hold on a just a sec...

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.160
There are more people sneaking
 out than usual today.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.460
Our door-unlocking ID can't
coincide with any of theirs, but...

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.030
You did it!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.550
Awesome! It's open!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:52.440
Sorry.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.130
I didn't get it quite right.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.690
That's the surveillance system?!

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.190
T-That's right!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.720
Be careful! These marks
are near permanent

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.530
and not easy to get rid of!

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.900
It's fine if you get one in a
place where you can hide it,

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.580
but forget about walking around
outside if you get one on your face!

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.210
They're...

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.300
...being chased too?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.080
Run!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.070
This way!

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.620
Kenneth! This is all your guys' fault!

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.640
It would seem that way.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.940
Thanks a lot. We were so close
to getting outside.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.930
Look out!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.430
Why you! How dare you!

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.040
Rajau...

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.500
It was an unfortunate accident.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.120
But this is a dangerous situation
we've gotten ourselves into.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:04.470
W-What now?

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.120
What do you mean, "What now?"

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.130
An aircar!

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.520
If we can just use that...

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.880
But there are too many people...

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.700
That was definitely cruel.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.800
We can't let their deaths be in vain!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.340
We have to have the time of our lives

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.700
while surrounded by beautiful girls!

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:36.810
It's our obligation to pay our fallen
comrades a tribute by doing so!

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:37.860
That's true!

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.740
Kenneth! Rajau!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.050
S-Seina-kun...

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:54.720
Forget about us and run! Hurry!

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.840
Seina! Have a night on the town.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.840
This is no time for goofing around!

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.560
It's up to me now!

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.280
Hey, Seina, pay attention when you drive!

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.950
I don't have a license!

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.450
What?!

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.560
Move! I'll drive!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.740
You can't!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.150
Hurry! Put it on Auto!

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.600
I wonder if it'll be okay.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.700
You mean about breaking the entrance?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.470
That along with a lot of other things.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.580
It'll be fine.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.380
The guys who helped us get
away'll be forced to fix it.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.560
It'll be fixed by the time we get back.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.210
But still...

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.810
Look! There it is!

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.260
Now are you glad you came?

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:08.720
The real fun is yet to come, though!

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.750
Say, girls!

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.020
Where you headed?

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.500
A party somewhere?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.510
W-Wait!

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.340
It's hopeless.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.180
What are you going to
do about those marks?

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.010
Dunno, they're not
very easy to get off.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.520
That's it! I have a great idea!

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.620
Now then, where shall we go?

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.550
Um, I don't know about this...

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:08.750
What's wrong?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.560
If it bothers you,
I can draw in some hair.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.890
T-That's not what I mean.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.730
Don't sweat the small stuff!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.400
It's what's on the inside
 that makes a man a man.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:20.760
That's right!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.910
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.880
Hey, Seina...

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:44.720
You got a girlfriend back on Earth?

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.390
You know, a girl you like.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.930
N-No...

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:49.310
How about you guys?

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.800
Me? Nope.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:56.640
I'm constantly looking
for someone new, you see.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.300
I don't have one either.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.820
I get the impression that liking
someone will take lots of time, so...

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.520
It's for that very reason that we braved danger

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.650
and escaped to find someone new.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.570
I see.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:12.350
The person of your destiny might
already be there waiting for you!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.580
What are you doing in
a place like this?

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.560
A-Amane-san?!

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.030
It's past your lights-out time.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:37.010
You're amazing! To think you
and Amane-san know each other!

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.640
What do you mean, amazing?

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.110
You mean you don't know?

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.980
Amane-san is the famous
daughter of the Kaunaq family,

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:45.220
and what's more, she was a top model!

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.060
I can't believe you know each other.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.740
Seina-kun, who are you?

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.990
Anyway, check this out.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:53.990
Pretty sweet, huh?

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:55.000
Y-Yes!

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:56.560
No.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:57.330
Kameo-san.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.600
Tsuruko-san.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:03.000
No way! The fact that Amane-san
brought us all here must mean...

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.370
W-What?! A foursome?!

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.220
What are you three
whispering about over there?

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:09.470
N-Nothing, really.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.180
How suspicious...

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:13.880
A-Amane-san...

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:14.650
What?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.480
I-Is it really okay for us
to come to a place like this?

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:20.750
Isn't that the reason why
you snuck out of the dorms?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:21.690
Um, well...

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:23.090
I knew it!

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.070
What do we do?!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.070
Let's have a toast first.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:30.280
To the brave heroes who overcame
the dorm security system.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.780
Cheers!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.340
What's wrong?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.340
Nothing.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.390
A-Amane-san!

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.350
Let your guard down and I'll get you.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:57.060
A-Amane-san,

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.430
You're acting a lot
different than usual today...

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.350
How so?

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:05.000
Well, I guess you're always
sort of flirtatious,

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.970
and you're loud and kind of moody,

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:11.360
but now you're kind of quieter, and nicer.

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.370
Maybe it's because of you, Seina-kun.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:18.580
Are you drunk, Amane-san?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.580
This is still my first glass.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.050
You boys drink up, too.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.540
R-Right!

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:30.720
To think that I would ever be
able to get near <i>the</i> Amane-san!

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.840
All of our pain and
suffering has paid off!

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.100
Oh, you mean you don't
want to go any further?

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.030
Say, do you have
any plans for tonight?

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:41.310
P-Plans?

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:43.230
The night has only begun.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.990
I'd like to show you

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.570
an even better place...

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.570
We have no plans! None at all! Nope!

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:51.280
That's right!

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.780
In that case, maybe
you'll come with me...

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.990
Y-Yes! We'd love to!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.050
Huh?

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:03.170
What is this? Some kind of play?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.950
A-Amane-san...

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:20.860
Seina-kun.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.940
Seina-kun!

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:27.770
Looks like you're awake.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.780
Amane-san!

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.980
What in the world is this?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.630
And I was so happy when I
thought my first experience

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:38.590
would be with Amane-san.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:42.560
Some things are just
too good to be true.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.560
Sorry.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.000
Amane-san?

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.600
You really are unlucky,

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.360
Yamada Seina-kun.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.470
Amane-san!

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.640
There's no need to be so shocked.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.980
It was a simple holographic field
utilizing a quasi-character program.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:07.750
I'm so lucky!

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.510
Don't I know you...

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.030
from before?

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.060
It looks like you remember me!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.630
But why are you doing this?

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.240
Um...

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.750
This wouldn't happen to be...

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:28.670
That's right.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:29.880
People-hunting.

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:31.320
People...

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.880
...hunting?

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.490
Hey, what's people-hunting?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.890
It basically means we're guinea pigs.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.320
For their human experiments.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.990
Human experiments?!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.160
No way!

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:04.160
Stop imaginin' stupid
stuff and get walkin'!

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:06.940
It's nothing to be that scared of.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.740
It's not like they used
to be a long time ago,

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:13.280
experiments nowadays are done
in highly advanced simulations.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.880
So even though they call
them human experiments,

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.250
they don't physically
do anything to your body.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.860
They use the data taken from
you to produce quasi-characters.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.140
Like that "Amane-san" just now.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:30.970
Then they do their
experiments on that data.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:33.840
But still, even if all
they do is take your data,

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.140
what if they do something
weird like they did just now?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.530
It's okay. You won't die.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.410
It's a good thing we were
the ones who caught you!

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:44.410
Had it been someone bad, who knows
what they would have used you for.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.210
Right?

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.580
Yes! We're so lucky!

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.690
Well, if children decide
to wander around at night,

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:53.590
it's their own fault if they
wind up in bad situations.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:57.560
Hey, Seina-kun, you know her too?

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:00.590
Y-Yeah. I think her name is Elma-san.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.230
What sort of relationship
do you two have?!

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:05.310
Are you two past the
cheek-rubbing stage?!

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:08.560
No. I've only met her once.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.840
I see.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.240
The academy's getting
better every day...

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.250
Ah. So her name's Elma-san...

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.070
Rajau.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.150
He said all that stuff earlier tonight,

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:22.210
but do you think he might actually
be the type who falls in love easily?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.870
Sorry to keep you waiting,
ladies and gentleman!

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.870
Today, we have a special treat - an always hard to come by Earthling.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:44.810
What's more, it's the notoriously unlucky boy, Yamada Seina-kun!

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.850
Let's all give him a
great round of applause!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:09.250
Welcome!! Test Subjects

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.870
They seem happy to see us.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.880
Okay! Preparations complete!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.010
Begin!

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.000
All done.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.700
Eh? I can go?

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.740
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:49.450
Seina-kun!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.950
Your friends are waiting
in the reception room.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.370
O-Okay.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.980
Well? That wasn't too bad, was it?

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:56.830
No, not really.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.090
Kenneth! Rajau!

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.420
Are you okay?!

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.160
Don't interrupt their experiments.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:10.730
But...

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:12.470
It's all right! See?

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:15.520
Wow! Hey, try touching here!

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:18.600
Wow! I didn't know young
ones were this amazing!

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.520
That's right!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:24.460
Seina! I'm all right!

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:26.330
You don't need to help!

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:31.450
Elma-san, I can't decide if
I want to be saved or not!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:38.540
You guys sure seem happy enough.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:43.190
To think that they would enjoy
being test subjects this much.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.660
Would you like to join them, Seina-kun?

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.970
No, uh...

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.970
Gimme a break, will ya!

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:00.230
Thank you for assisting
us in our experiments.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:02.080
N-No, thank you!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.570
Elma-san! If you ever need help,
I'll always be happy to assist!

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.680
I just might ask you again sometime!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.700
Bye, Seina-kun.

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.070
Yes!

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.140
Bye, Elma-san!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.620
Let's make it just you and me next time!

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:20.000
Man, what a great night!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.630
And it's all thanks to Seina!

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.630
That was so amazing!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.720
What in the world happened?!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.050
Oh, Elma-san, it's terrible!

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.150
It's Yamada Seina-kun's personal data.

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:43.270
It made it onto the outside
network through a security hole!

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.490
What's more, it was infected by
a virus we've never seen before,

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:49.730
and then it broke into our servers
and destroyed all of our data!

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:52.660
This is Seina-kun's unluckiness...

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:56.230
We physically cut our server
off from the outside network,

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.830
but Yamada Seina-kun's personal data...

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.160
You can't find it?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.870
Correct. It's been 48 minutes
and 22 seconds since we lost it.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.670
We even have Airi-sama
assisting us now, but...

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.310
I've located Yamada Seina!

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:08.670
I've successfully captured him!

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:11.540
I'll bring him out right now!

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:21.940
Who the hell're you?!
Whatchoo lookin' at, fool?! Hey!

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:26.900
Judging from how long we'd lost his data,
the hard part is yet to begin...

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:30.610
That's right! Seina's really popular with the girls!

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:34.270
He was like, "Yeah, I'm really
glad I came into space!"

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.700
What a bad situation...

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:43.080
Will this really never come off?

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:45.280
Oh, perfect timing!

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.420
We were just talking about you!

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.090
With who?

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.860
K-Kiriko-san!

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:55.390
It looks like you're really
enjoying yourself, Seina-chan.

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:56.180
Kiriko-san!

00:21:58.730 --> 00:22:01.030
Hey. At least put a paper bag on.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:02.480
Yeah, how rude.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.590
Kiriko-san!

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:21.660
uchuu de saitei saiaku

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:21.660
You're the worst, most hopeless,

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:26.780
un warui Unlucky Boy

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:26.780
most unlucky boy in space.

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:33.990
anna koto shite te mo

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:33.990
No matter what you do,

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:36.720
konna koto shite te mo

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:36.720
no matter what you do,

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:41.510
otozureru jiko tensai sugoi wana

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:41.510
you can't escape the accidents, disasters and traps

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:43.800
anata wa nigerarenai

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:43.800
that come your way.

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.370
keikai shite te mo

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.370
Even if your really careful...

00:22:48.350 --> 00:22:50.080
ikinari shichatte mo

00:22:48.350 --> 00:22:50.080
And even if you're not...

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:56.310
saitei saiaku dame dame no

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:56.310
You're the worst and most hopeless...

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:00.780
anata wa doshiyou mo nai

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:00.780
You're a lost cause.

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:10.730
anata ga saitei saiaku

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:10.730
You're the worst and most hopeless...

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:15.350
anata wa Unlucky Boy

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:15.350
You're an unlucky boy.

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:20.430
dakedo anata shika mienai

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:20.430
But all I can see is you,

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:25.950
sonna anata shika mienai

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:25.950
just the way you are.

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.670
The GP Academy entrance
ceremony has taken place,

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.070
and classes have begun with
almost no time to spare.

00:23:36.070 --> 00:23:38.970
The instructor for basic
training is Seiryo Tennan-sensei.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:41.580
But he doesn't need to
keep his eye on me so much!

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:43.650
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!
